1
00:00:49,984 --> 00:00:52,034
This is where I begin, isn't it?

2
00:00:52,944 --> 00:00:54,974
To make my wish come true.

3
00:00:57,684 --> 00:00:59,674
I, Kobato... am ready!

4
00:01:05,664 --> 00:01:08,794
Kobato.

5
00:01:08,794 --> 00:01:11,634
Kobato.
What should I do?

6
00:01:11,634 --> 00:01:16,034
Kobato.
Even the most obvious of things

7
00:01:16,944 --> 00:01:20,244
Are always such a challenge

8
00:01:20,244 --> 00:01:23,014
I want to laugh when I'm happy

9
00:01:23,014 --> 00:01:27,314
And sing whenever I want

10
00:01:27,884 --> 00:01:30,314
Is all

11
00:01:31,624 --> 00:01:35,994
They say my dreams will come true someday

12
00:01:36,424 --> 00:01:39,694
But when will "someday" come?

13
00:01:39,694 --> 00:01:43,184
I can't wait forever

14
00:01:43,334 --> 00:01:49,104
On "1, 2, 3!" I'll spread open my arms

15
00:01:49,104 --> 00:01:54,314
And let the light gather around me

16
00:01:54,314 --> 00:01:57,144
Where is it?

17
00:01:57,144 --> 00:02:00,484
Please tell me what I can do

18
00:02:00,484 --> 00:02:03,314
I make the most of getting hurt

19
00:02:03,314 --> 00:02:06,224
And run with all my might

20
00:02:06,224 --> 00:02:10,194
Despite how many dozens of times I fall

21
00:02:10,194 --> 00:02:13,224
And start crying

22
00:02:13,224 --> 00:02:17,254
I surprise myself

23
00:02:17,734 --> 00:02:21,894
In how much I believe in tomorrow

24
00:02:33,554 --> 00:02:36,454
...A Girl's Wish.

25
00:02:36,454 --> 00:02:37,584
...A Girl's Wish.
Kobato...

26
00:02:38,254 --> 00:02:40,184
Yes, Ioryogi-san.

27
00:02:40,654 --> 00:02:42,644
We have finally arrived.

28
00:02:42,954 --> 00:02:45,464
This is the Ningenkai, where people live.

29
00:02:45,464 --> 00:02:46,894
You do understand that?

30
00:02:46,894 --> 00:02:48,764
Yes, I do.

31
00:02:49,164 --> 00:02:53,694
And for your wish to come true, well that all
depends on how hard you try here in Ningenkai.

32
00:02:54,134 --> 00:02:55,904
You understand that, too.

33
00:02:56,074 --> 00:02:57,904
Yes, of course!

34
00:02:59,004 --> 00:03:01,034
Well, if you understand

35
00:03:02,674 --> 00:03:06,974
Then why are we stuffed in this hole
immediately upon our arrival?!

36
00:03:07,384 --> 00:03:10,984
But... but I thought it would be
fun if we could hide out,

37
00:03:10,984 --> 00:03:13,614
kinda like a secret meeting or something...

38
00:03:19,494 --> 00:03:21,864
We didn't come here so you could have fun!

39
00:03:24,534 --> 00:03:25,934
Kobato Hanato!

40
00:03:25,934 --> 00:03:26,904
Yes sir!

41
00:03:26,904 --> 00:03:28,174
What is your wish?

42
00:03:28,174 --> 00:03:29,904
There's a place I want to go!

43
00:03:30,274 --> 00:03:32,934
And what did he tell you you need
to do before you could do that?!

44
00:03:33,244 --> 00:03:36,804
I must collect a "bottle full of broken hearts"!

45
00:03:37,314 --> 00:03:38,434
Before that?!

46
00:03:38,714 --> 00:03:41,304
I need you to give me the "bottle"!

47
00:03:41,514 --> 00:03:43,004
To get that "bottle"?!

48
00:03:43,314 --> 00:03:47,094
I need to pass a test to see if
I'm worthy of living here!

49
00:03:47,094 --> 00:03:48,354
Exactly!

50
00:03:48,354 --> 00:03:50,994
I am going to spend the day today,

51
00:03:50,994 --> 00:03:53,084
checking to see if you have enough
common sense to live in the Ningenkai!

52
00:03:53,324 --> 00:03:55,294
The test has already begun!

53
00:03:55,294 --> 00:03:58,024
Under the supervision and verdict of yours truly!

54
00:03:59,764 --> 00:04:01,204
Do you hear me young lady?!

55
00:04:01,204 --> 00:04:02,794
Y-Yes sir I understand... sir.

56
00:04:03,274 --> 00:04:08,404
Your test will be judged on how
well you can behave "here".

57
00:04:08,844 --> 00:04:11,544
Now go, Kobato!

58
00:04:11,714 --> 00:04:15,044
Go and do the right things,
in this park where spring has come!

59
00:04:17,154 --> 00:04:18,484
What are you waiting for?!

60
00:04:19,054 --> 00:04:20,114
Yes sir!

61
00:04:31,764 --> 00:04:33,824
So, what do you think, Ioryogi-san?

62
00:04:35,304 --> 00:04:38,764
Are you a basket worm hibernating until spring?!

63
00:04:41,414 --> 00:04:42,814
Give me a break...

64
00:04:43,514 --> 00:04:46,884
Are you saying you can't even
act naturally in a park?

65
00:04:47,414 --> 00:04:49,114
I'm sorry.

66
00:04:49,314 --> 00:04:50,884
You're impossible.

67
00:04:50,884 --> 00:04:54,614
Why couldn't you at least take the trash out?

68
00:04:56,694 --> 00:04:58,024
I'm going to miss my bus!

69
00:05:00,094 --> 00:05:01,224
Excuse me!

70
00:05:01,464 --> 00:05:02,194
No, not at all.

71
00:05:03,264 --> 00:05:05,534
Oh no! I'm going to be late for work!

72
00:05:07,934 --> 00:05:09,074
Ioryogi-san.

73
00:05:09,074 --> 00:05:10,504
Looks like she dropped it.

74
00:05:11,704 --> 00:05:13,734
Perfect. Here's the next test.

75
00:05:14,174 --> 00:05:15,164
Huh?

76
00:05:16,614 --> 00:05:20,744
Let's see what you're going
to do now with that trash.

77
00:05:20,884 --> 00:05:22,614
Y-Yes sir.

78
00:05:24,954 --> 00:05:26,784
Garbage disposal...

79
00:05:26,994 --> 00:05:28,894
Where's the garbage disposal?

80
00:05:31,094 --> 00:05:32,754
I found it!

81
00:05:36,934 --> 00:05:38,064
Here...

82
00:05:38,064 --> 00:05:39,304
Here?

83
00:05:39,304 --> 00:05:40,404
I'll put this...

84
00:05:40,404 --> 00:05:41,834
You'll put this?

85
00:05:43,104 --> 00:05:44,534
Please cooperate in reducing garbage.

86
00:05:44,604 --> 00:05:47,074
Please cooperate in reducing garbage.

87
00:05:54,254 --> 00:05:55,614
The crows...

88
00:05:55,984 --> 00:05:57,744
They're probably after the garbage.

89
00:05:58,024 --> 00:06:00,214
They'll start picking at you if you don't hurry.

90
00:06:01,794 --> 00:06:03,254
They're after...

91
00:06:04,424 --> 00:06:05,914
The crows...

92
00:06:06,624 --> 00:06:07,924
They want the garbage...

93
00:06:22,374 --> 00:06:24,644
Here you are, crows!

94
00:06:28,954 --> 00:06:30,644
What are you doing!?

95
00:06:39,594 --> 00:06:41,234
That surprised me.

96
00:06:41,234 --> 00:06:44,024
What was the big idea, calling the crows over?!

97
00:06:44,334 --> 00:06:46,534
But the crows, they seemed to be hungry.

98
00:06:46,534 --> 00:06:48,834
And it said right on the sign, to reduce trash.

99
00:06:48,904 --> 00:06:50,574
I'm no longer calling you Kobato!

100
00:06:50,574 --> 00:06:52,204
"Dobato" is a good enough name for you!

101
00:06:52,544 --> 00:06:54,474
That's not nice.

102
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:56,374
Hey, sweetie.

103
00:06:57,184 --> 00:06:58,704
Are you here alone?

104
00:06:59,014 --> 00:07:00,814
Wanna go for coffee?

105
00:07:01,954 --> 00:07:02,914
Coffee?

106
00:07:02,914 --> 00:07:05,684
There's a cool place down the street.

107
00:07:05,924 --> 00:07:08,584
Yeah, right. Picking up girls in mid-afternoon?

108
00:07:09,124 --> 00:07:10,594
We'll pay.

109
00:07:10,594 --> 00:07:11,794
You're buying?!

110
00:07:11,794 --> 00:07:13,384
Thank you very much!

111
00:07:13,734 --> 00:07:15,664
Cool, shall we go then?

112
00:07:15,664 --> 00:07:16,754
Okay!

113
00:07:16,864 --> 00:07:19,024
Aren't we lucky, Ioryogi-san?

114
00:07:21,704 --> 00:07:23,224
Are you out of your mind?!

115
00:07:23,404 --> 00:07:25,704
What the heck did you come here to do?!

116
00:07:25,704 --> 00:07:27,644
What? But they're going to treat us...

117
00:07:28,744 --> 00:07:30,674
Are you okay?!

118
00:07:31,584 --> 00:07:33,104
Are you hurt?

119
00:07:33,954 --> 00:07:36,514
Hey! What did you just do to us?!

120
00:07:37,084 --> 00:07:38,314
Huh?

121
00:07:40,994 --> 00:07:43,254
Hey! Who do you think
you're messing with?!

122
00:07:54,234 --> 00:07:56,964
You guys get on my nerves.

123
00:08:00,974 --> 00:08:02,804
Oh man, she was with a guy!

124
00:08:07,584 --> 00:08:09,244
U-Um...

125
00:08:09,784 --> 00:08:10,214
Thank y-

126
00:08:10,214 --> 00:08:10,824
Don't flatter yourself just because
some guy was kind to you.
Thank y-

127
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:12,724
Don't flatter yourself just because
some guy was kind to you.

128
00:08:18,194 --> 00:08:20,024
What?!

129
00:08:20,024 --> 00:08:21,994
I wasn't flattering myself!

130
00:08:22,964 --> 00:08:25,204
Well, you looked pretty happy.

131
00:08:25,204 --> 00:08:27,394
Anyone would misunderstand.

132
00:08:37,814 --> 00:08:40,214
I'm so glad it's such a nice day!

133
00:08:40,454 --> 00:08:42,114
A lot of customers here to view the flowers.

134
00:08:42,114 --> 00:08:43,944
It's going to get busy!

135
00:08:44,124 --> 00:08:45,284
Isn't it, Fujimoto?

136
00:08:45,284 --> 00:08:46,624
Yes it is.

137
00:08:46,624 --> 00:08:48,554
Oh, can you take these out?

138
00:08:49,094 --> 00:08:50,144
Sure.

139
00:08:51,324 --> 00:08:52,494
That cat was really cute.

140
00:08:52,494 --> 00:08:53,424
Here you are.
That cat was really cute.

141
00:08:54,264 --> 00:08:56,064
Let me take these away for you.

142
00:08:56,364 --> 00:08:57,764
Oh, thanks.

143
00:08:59,634 --> 00:09:01,004
He's cool!

144
00:09:01,174 --> 00:09:03,474
I hear you. You wanna ask him his name?

145
00:09:03,474 --> 00:09:04,404
What?

146
00:09:05,604 --> 00:09:08,134
You could show them a little service.

147
00:09:08,344 --> 00:09:11,144
At least smile or something.
The girls would be all over you.

148
00:09:11,144 --> 00:09:13,544
I'm not interested in having girls come after me.

149
00:09:13,644 --> 00:09:15,584
What a dude.

150
00:09:19,324 --> 00:09:22,184
I'm sorry. I forgot to turn it off.

151
00:09:23,894 --> 00:09:26,824
Yomogi Kindergarten

152
00:09:28,564 --> 00:09:30,154
Hello, Fujimoto speaking.

153
00:09:30,394 --> 00:09:32,234
What's the matter, Ms. Sayaka?

154
00:09:34,974 --> 00:09:36,594
They showed up at the kindergarten again?!

155
00:09:37,474 --> 00:09:39,834
Hang on, I'll be there as soon as I can!

156
00:09:40,544 --> 00:09:41,914
Sir, something has come up!

157
00:09:41,914 --> 00:09:43,104
I've got to get somewhere right away.

158
00:09:50,184 --> 00:09:51,414
I wonder what's going on.

159
00:09:51,484 --> 00:09:53,974
Look at all the people over there, Ioryogi-san.

160
00:09:54,294 --> 00:09:56,624
Could be a flower viewing festival.

161
00:09:57,724 --> 00:10:00,954
Whatever it is, something sure smells good!

162
00:10:01,464 --> 00:10:02,934
Let's go take a look.

163
00:10:03,064 --> 00:10:05,464
Yes. Let's do that.

164
00:10:10,374 --> 00:10:12,034
Wow!

165
00:10:12,674 --> 00:10:14,404
They're in full bloom.

166
00:10:15,244 --> 00:10:17,144
They're so beautiful!

167
00:10:20,754 --> 00:10:23,044
Miss, can you get the ball?

168
00:10:23,884 --> 00:10:25,784
Uh, sure!

169
00:10:26,024 --> 00:10:27,594
Okay!

170
00:10:27,594 --> 00:10:29,924
Thank you very much!

171
00:10:30,294 --> 00:10:32,194
Here I go.

172
00:10:33,294 --> 00:10:34,784
There!

173
00:10:38,234 --> 00:10:40,034
Woah! Wh-What was that?!

174
00:10:41,504 --> 00:10:42,864
I'm sorry!

175
00:10:43,274 --> 00:10:44,744
Guess it couldn't be helped...

176
00:10:44,744 --> 00:10:46,734
Really, I am so sorry!

177
00:10:47,874 --> 00:10:50,364
I'm short staffed as it is...

178
00:10:52,884 --> 00:10:54,674
Please let me help you!

179
00:10:54,914 --> 00:10:56,074
Huh?

180
00:10:56,354 --> 00:10:58,514
Let me make it up to you by helping, please!

181
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:00,014
What?

182
00:11:11,734 --> 00:11:13,704
Can I get another beer, please?

183
00:11:14,204 --> 00:11:15,304
Roger!

184
00:11:15,304 --> 00:11:18,434
My waiter suddenly had to go home, you see.

185
00:11:18,904 --> 00:11:19,744
You're such a great help, thank you.

186
00:11:19,744 --> 00:11:21,334
Really?

187
00:11:21,474 --> 00:11:23,774
I am so happy to be of help to you!

188
00:11:24,884 --> 00:11:27,044
To be of help is a rarity for Kobato.

189
00:11:27,914 --> 00:11:30,184
Excuse me. Is our hot pot ready yet?

190
00:11:30,414 --> 00:11:31,904
Yes sir, right away!

191
00:11:32,054 --> 00:11:33,484
Please take this over to them.

192
00:11:33,854 --> 00:11:34,954
Are you listening to me?

193
00:11:34,954 --> 00:11:35,924
Sure I'm listening.

194
00:11:35,924 --> 00:11:36,624
Here you are!
Sure I'm listening.

195
00:11:37,364 --> 00:11:39,664
Oh thanks. Could you stew it for us?

196
00:11:39,664 --> 00:11:40,424
Huh?

197
00:11:40,424 --> 00:11:41,724
Thank you!

198
00:11:41,964 --> 00:11:43,564
So you see...

199
00:11:43,564 --> 00:11:44,934
Yes, you were saying?

200
00:11:47,474 --> 00:11:51,064
You want me to stew it in the hot pot?

201
00:11:52,604 --> 00:11:54,504
This will be a good thing to test.

202
00:11:55,144 --> 00:11:59,244
Let's take a look at how well le chef
Kobato handles the hot pot!

203
00:12:03,054 --> 00:12:03,954
There!

204
00:12:03,954 --> 00:12:07,384
Wh-What the? The water's not even boiling.
Don't put anything in yet.

205
00:12:08,854 --> 00:12:11,344
Oh no, not the meat! No, not yet!

206
00:12:12,394 --> 00:12:14,334
Now why on earth would you add milk?!

207
00:12:14,334 --> 00:12:16,164
Why not? It's healthy!

208
00:12:17,364 --> 00:12:18,834
Woah, hold the chocolate bar!

209
00:12:18,834 --> 00:12:20,764
Eating sweets gives you energy!

210
00:12:22,034 --> 00:12:23,874
No! Not natto!

211
00:12:23,874 --> 00:12:25,464
Yikes!

212
00:12:31,914 --> 00:12:34,574
Looks like a painting of hell...

213
00:12:37,384 --> 00:12:39,784
B-But it would be a waste not to... hm?

214
00:12:42,424 --> 00:12:43,614
Huh?

215
00:12:44,294 --> 00:12:45,384
Delicious!

216
00:12:50,034 --> 00:12:51,334
You know, it is!

217
00:12:51,334 --> 00:12:52,824
Give it a try, you'd be surprised!

218
00:12:53,334 --> 00:12:54,324
Huh?

219
00:12:56,704 --> 00:12:57,904
This is good.

220
00:12:59,944 --> 00:13:01,344
It really is.

221
00:13:01,344 --> 00:13:02,474
Great!

222
00:13:02,474 --> 00:13:03,964
Delicious!

223
00:13:04,984 --> 00:13:07,844
Young lady, I'm going to put
this on my regular menu.

224
00:13:08,554 --> 00:13:10,484
Thank you so much!

225
00:13:11,084 --> 00:13:13,024
You're pretty good for a young lady.

226
00:13:13,754 --> 00:13:16,454
Now you've made me want to try some.

227
00:13:17,394 --> 00:13:19,584
You're just a Dobato, and a cheeky one at that.

228
00:13:36,174 --> 00:13:39,904
Kobato, as far as hot pot knowledge
is concerned, you get a zero.

229
00:13:40,014 --> 00:13:41,004
What?!

230
00:13:41,354 --> 00:13:46,084
But in the end you concocted something that
actually tasted good, so I'll give you forty.

231
00:13:46,884 --> 00:13:48,284
Is that all?

232
00:13:56,964 --> 00:13:59,834
Here you go, honey. How do you like that?

233
00:14:06,174 --> 00:14:07,574
What's the matter?

234
00:14:08,974 --> 00:14:11,534
She won't stop crying.

235
00:14:25,894 --> 00:14:27,634
Aw, I'm sorry!

236
00:14:27,634 --> 00:14:29,764
Oh dear, it's not your fault.

237
00:14:29,764 --> 00:14:31,234
Don't let it worry you.

238
00:14:31,234 --> 00:14:32,464
But...

239
00:14:32,464 --> 00:14:35,494
This child is always like this at night.

240
00:14:35,874 --> 00:14:40,674
I often bring her here to the park so that
she doesn't keep the neighbors awake.

241
00:14:40,844 --> 00:14:43,344
She just won't go to sleep until
she tires herself out crying.

242
00:14:43,344 --> 00:14:44,934
Oh, is that right?

243
00:14:45,244 --> 00:14:52,224
Her mother used to be by her side all the time
and sang to her when she started up like this.

244
00:14:52,224 --> 00:14:54,884
Then she'd settle down.

245
00:14:55,994 --> 00:14:58,454
Where is her mother now?

246
00:14:59,024 --> 00:15:03,364
Right now, she's out working hard for the baby.

247
00:15:03,534 --> 00:15:07,694
That's why I have to take good care of her.

248
00:15:10,174 --> 00:15:16,074
But an old lady's singing doesn't
help to settle her down.

249
00:15:18,714 --> 00:15:20,074
Let me sing to her!

250
00:15:21,354 --> 00:15:22,584
What?

251
00:15:22,584 --> 00:15:25,174
Let me sing for the baby!

252
00:15:25,724 --> 00:15:29,744
Though I probably can't sing like her mother.

253
00:15:37,534 --> 00:15:39,224
Could you, then?

254
00:15:41,174 --> 00:15:42,294
Yes!

255
00:15:48,974 --> 00:15:51,574
I'll try to sing my very best.

256
00:16:02,254 --> 00:16:08,164
Flowers blossom in the spring

257
00:16:08,864 --> 00:16:14,764
Skies in the summer reach far and wide

258
00:16:15,434 --> 00:16:19,974
Every time I think of this

259
00:16:19,974 --> 00:16:21,414
I'm all right. I just got back to work.
Every time I think of this

260
00:16:21,414 --> 00:16:22,014
I'm all right. I just got back to work.

261
00:16:22,014 --> 00:16:23,514
I'm all right. I just got back to work.
Precious thoughts spread across in my heart

262
00:16:23,514 --> 00:16:24,144
Precious thoughts spread across in my heart

263
00:16:24,144 --> 00:16:26,544
Please don't worry about a thing, Ms. Sayaka.
Precious thoughts spread across in my heart

264
00:16:26,544 --> 00:16:28,014
Precious thoughts spread across in my heart

265
00:16:28,514 --> 00:16:31,684
In the morning when it rains

266
00:16:31,684 --> 00:16:33,684
Uh, no, there's this song...
In the morning when it rains

267
00:16:33,684 --> 00:16:35,024
In the morning when it rains

268
00:16:35,024 --> 00:16:40,864
On those days when the windows stay closed

269
00:16:41,594 --> 00:16:47,764
My heart shimmers with the light

270
00:16:48,104 --> 00:16:54,374
Light shining brightly above the clouds

271
00:16:55,714 --> 00:17:02,084
The voices are calling to me

272
00:17:02,284 --> 00:17:08,654
From way over yonder, from far I can hear

273
00:17:08,854 --> 00:17:12,664
Voices of laughter

274
00:17:12,664 --> 00:17:15,664
Voices of singing

275
00:17:15,664 --> 00:17:21,664
Echoing voices of the wind

276
00:17:21,934 --> 00:17:25,204
In happiness and in sadness

277
00:17:25,204 --> 00:17:27,244
Well, I'll have to give her credit for singing.
In happiness and in sadness

278
00:17:27,244 --> 00:17:28,414
She does it very well.
In happiness and in sadness

279
00:17:28,414 --> 00:17:29,244
In all I behold and all that I live for

280
00:17:29,244 --> 00:17:31,984
I guess that goes for Kohaku, too.
In all I behold and all that I live for

281
00:17:31,984 --> 00:17:34,984
In all I behold and all that I live for

282
00:17:34,984 --> 00:17:38,754
With my hand in your hand

283
00:17:38,754 --> 00:17:41,794
Your hand in my hand

284
00:17:41,794 --> 00:17:48,594
Together, we are one and whole

285
00:18:01,474 --> 00:18:03,634
Um... Um, I...

286
00:18:05,314 --> 00:18:07,374
That was quite nice.

287
00:18:07,714 --> 00:18:10,114
The baby seems to have stopped crying.

288
00:18:17,524 --> 00:18:18,994
I'm so glad.

289
00:18:20,424 --> 00:18:22,424
Thanks to you, dear.

290
00:18:22,534 --> 00:18:24,394
Hey sing us another one!

291
00:18:24,634 --> 00:18:25,964
We want to hear more!

292
00:18:25,964 --> 00:18:29,204
Yeah, more! Please!

293
00:18:29,204 --> 00:18:30,034
What? What?! What?!!

294
00:18:30,034 --> 00:18:32,164
There's a stage over there! Come on let's go!

295
00:18:47,424 --> 00:18:50,684
We got all these gifts from those people.

296
00:18:51,164 --> 00:18:54,684
Well they said it was for your singing.
May as well keep it.

297
00:18:56,634 --> 00:19:01,274
Um... so, so! How did I do on the test?

298
00:19:01,274 --> 00:19:04,534
Huh? Oh, the test...

299
00:19:07,704 --> 00:19:09,374
Kobato Hanato!

300
00:19:09,544 --> 00:19:11,014
Y-Y-Y-Yes sir!

301
00:19:11,644 --> 00:19:17,714
In the first half, you were totally wild and
unpredictable and in the second half,

302
00:19:17,714 --> 00:19:19,844
well that hot pot was a product of luck.

303
00:19:20,854 --> 00:19:22,914
But your singing was okay...

304
00:19:23,094 --> 00:19:24,354
Uh, then...

305
00:19:24,494 --> 00:19:25,754
You fail!

306
00:19:27,934 --> 00:19:31,034
But you said my singing was okay!

307
00:19:31,034 --> 00:19:32,704
The first half was just too much of a mess!

308
00:19:32,704 --> 00:19:35,234
Aw, come on!

309
00:19:35,234 --> 00:19:37,304
You're mean. You're just too mean!

310
00:19:37,304 --> 00:19:39,704
I really tried, you know!

311
00:19:39,704 --> 00:19:43,074
Well, you almost made it. Too bad!

312
00:19:43,314 --> 00:19:44,934
Oh please!

313
00:19:45,244 --> 00:19:46,734
Dear?

314
00:19:47,784 --> 00:19:50,054
Oh you're the grandmother
from earlier this evening.

315
00:19:50,054 --> 00:19:51,524
Good evening.

316
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:55,044
Good evening, young lady
with the beautiful voice.

317
00:19:55,794 --> 00:19:57,724
I'm so happy to see you again.

318
00:20:00,564 --> 00:20:02,964
Thank you so much for earlier.

319
00:20:05,464 --> 00:20:07,904
I just wanted to offer you a word of thanks.

320
00:20:07,904 --> 00:20:13,034
That was the first time the baby enjoyed
someone other than her mother singing for her.

321
00:20:13,544 --> 00:20:18,704
She was having such a great time and the
next moment, she'd fallen asleep.

322
00:20:19,614 --> 00:20:25,354
I wanted to stay and thank you for what you
did for her, but I had to take her home.

323
00:20:25,354 --> 00:20:26,914
Sorry for leaving without a word.

324
00:20:27,084 --> 00:20:29,284
Oh no, there's no need to be sorry.

325
00:20:30,224 --> 00:20:33,664
Your singing was truly wonderful.

326
00:20:34,564 --> 00:20:37,034
Please let me hear you again sometime.

327
00:20:37,364 --> 00:20:39,024
Wh-Why sure.

328
00:20:39,104 --> 00:20:41,294
Good night, then.

329
00:20:41,574 --> 00:20:44,334
Oh, yes, good night.

330
00:20:55,884 --> 00:20:57,214
Hm?

331
00:21:00,424 --> 00:21:02,184
Kobato Hanato!

332
00:21:02,554 --> 00:21:03,684
Yes sir!

333
00:21:12,134 --> 00:21:13,694
You pass.

334
00:21:14,164 --> 00:21:15,654
Huh?

335
00:21:40,324 --> 00:21:42,194
Why, this is...

336
00:21:42,394 --> 00:21:44,524
...the bottle, isn't it?

337
00:21:44,604 --> 00:21:45,964
Yep.

338
00:21:45,964 --> 00:21:47,704
It is the real thing, isn't it?

339
00:21:47,704 --> 00:21:48,674
Yes it is.

340
00:21:48,674 --> 00:21:52,404
That grandmother's gratitude to you
brings you up to a score of 100.

341
00:21:52,404 --> 00:21:54,174
You have passed the test.

342
00:21:54,504 --> 00:21:57,674
Is it really, really, really... the real thing?

343
00:21:57,674 --> 00:21:58,914
If you don't want it, give it back!

344
00:21:58,914 --> 00:22:01,574
No, no! I want it, I want it!

345
00:22:05,924 --> 00:22:11,454
So if I heal broken hearts and collect the
pieces in this bottle until it's full...

346
00:22:12,694 --> 00:22:14,524
Your wish will come true.

347
00:22:15,094 --> 00:22:17,654
But you've only just gotten the bottle.

348
00:22:17,934 --> 00:22:18,994
Yes.

349
00:22:19,104 --> 00:22:21,894
Kobato Hanato! What is your wish?!

350
00:22:23,374 --> 00:22:25,274
There's a place I want to go.

351
00:22:25,844 --> 00:22:27,674
Before you can do that, what do you need?

352
00:22:28,644 --> 00:22:33,134
I must fill this bottle with broken hearts.

353
00:22:33,744 --> 00:22:38,374
Okay. Now. It's show time. This is only the
beginning. There's a long way to go!

354
00:22:38,684 --> 00:22:41,954
Yes sir! I'm ready!

355
00:22:42,854 --> 00:22:46,764
Get that smirk off of your face. You'd better
know what you're up against, Dobato!

356
00:22:46,764 --> 00:22:46,864
Aw, that's not nice!

357
00:22:46,864 --> 00:22:48,934
Dobato
Aw, that's not nice!

358
00:22:48,934 --> 00:22:52,204
Dobato
My name is Kobato! Kobato Hanato!

359
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:53,464
Dobato
Dobato's good enough for you!

360
00:22:53,464 --> 00:22:53,604
Dobato's good enough for you!

361
00:22:53,604 --> 00:22:54,874
If you don't like that, it's Dabada!

362
00:22:54,874 --> 00:22:54,974
Dabada
If you don't like that, it's Dabada!

363
00:22:54,974 --> 00:22:55,074
Dabada

364
00:22:55,074 --> 00:22:57,304
Dabada
What?! Dabada?!

365
00:22:57,304 --> 00:22:57,704
Dabada

366
00:23:01,274 --> 00:23:08,914
Everyone dreams of flying

367
00:23:10,084 --> 00:23:16,184
But they let gravity trick them

368
00:23:16,454 --> 00:23:24,294
Honestly, everyone is already able to fly

369
00:23:26,534 --> 00:23:32,874
I bet the reason that child looks so terribly sad

370
00:23:33,904 --> 00:23:36,774
Is because he

371
00:23:36,774 --> 00:23:43,914
Accidentally lost his shadow somewhere

372
00:23:44,084 --> 00:23:46,614
In that case

373
00:23:46,784 --> 00:23:50,894
If I could just tell you, "Thank you,"

374
00:23:50,894 --> 00:23:54,764
And you laugh and reply, "Thank you"

375
00:23:54,764 --> 00:24:02,104
That exchange would fill you with joy

376
00:24:02,634 --> 00:24:06,864
It would make you feel so happy

377
00:24:07,174 --> 00:24:11,414
There's nothing to worry about

378
00:24:11,414 --> 00:24:15,504
Since we're together

379
00:24:17,284 --> 00:24:23,224
It's strange how I'm crying

380
00:24:23,224 --> 00:24:26,024
Even though I'm happy

381
00:24:26,024 --> 00:24:28,964
Next episode
...The Shining Kompeito.
Even though I'm happy

382
00:24:28,964 --> 00:24:30,764
Next episode
...The Shining Kompeito.

